This setup will catch errors for you in real time, it tells you why it's an error so you can fix it, and it highlights *possible* problems as warnings.  

If you pull a v1 script into vs code and mark it as v2, it'll tell you every single syntactical error (things written incorrectly) in the file.  
If you have classic syntax, it'll flag it for being incorrect.  
It knows when you're trying to use command syntax and will tell you.  
It does a lot without you even having to ask it to.

Along with all the error detection stuff, it provides every function name, built-in variable name, class/method/property name, and more.   
While typing, you'll get an autocomplete window that uses a fuzzy search to find what you're looking for.  
Want `WinGetMinMax`? Type `WinGetM` and you'll see it. Or get even shorter and do `wgmm` and WinGetMinMax() will be the only thing that comes up (barring any user functions of course).  

Not only that, it will favor things that are in scope (accessible).  
If what you're typing isn't in scope, it'll still suggest other spellings that it finds in the file.  

The addon also keeps track of object info like properties.  
Example: If  you make an object and it has properties `a`, `b`, and `c` in it and you go to use that object, [it'll show `a`, `b`, `c` in the autocomplete](https://i.imgur.com/lBfqlGR.png) list.  

If you let it, VS Code and the ahk v2 addon will type the bulk of the characters in your code for you just from autocomplete.  

