# - Let's talk about the new classes in v2!

First of all, [this is one of my favorite AHK doc pages]().  
It shows the entire object structure of the language.  
As you learn more about v2, this page makes more and more sense.  
But it shows you all the classes.  

What's a class? It's 2 things.  
It can be a big container to store associated things or they can be used to generate objects.  
They can be used for one, the other, or both. They're dual functioning.

The AHK-provided classes lets us create "objects", or bundles, for our code.  
An object can have properties, which act like it's own personal variables.  
it also can have methods, which act like it's own personal variables.  

Take GUIs for example.  
In v1, there were generalized commands for making generic guis and you had to track handles or, worse, people would just use global variables as variables for gui elements.  
